impl.summary:
The branch is based on perf2/win-hdr-desktop (600eea0). Files under /Users/lb7666/rust_pro/pb-mapper/.claude/worktrees/wf_352d1379-280-61:

- crates/pb-mapper-desktop/src/codec/refine.rs (new): the neutral `Repeats` policy, with an injected clock, and 7 tests. A burst starts REFINE_AFTER = 200 ms (const-asserted below LIVENESS_INTERVAL) after a fresh unit (a new picture or a keyframe) that filled at least 3/4 of a frame's budget (bitrate / 8 / nominal fps). Repeats go at least one pace period apart. A burst ends at the first of:
  - two non-keyframe outputs in a row under 512 B, once it has had REFINE_MIN = 3 outputs;
  - two outputs that did not lower the QP, after the same 3 outputs;
  - a QP at or below REFINE_QP_FLOOR = 18;
  - REFINE_MAX = 15 repeats of the picture, counted across interruptions;
  - REFINE_MAX_TIME = 1 s.
  A new picture or keyframe ends the burst. Outputs older than the burst's first repeat are ignored. A pace of 4 fps or slower runs no burst. Liveness follows unchanged. The API is `fresh`, `refined`, `output(pts, duplicate, keyframe, len, qp)`, `next_due` and `repeat_now -> Option<Repeat>`.
- codec/present_waiter.rs: `Idle` carries `repeats`. `repeat_due` and `until` use `Repeats::next_due` and `repeat_now`, and the new `refines(now)` tells a refinement repeat. Tests: the refinement schedule and the no-spin property, now with a burst as well.
- platform/windows/video/mod.rs:
  - new `Submit::Refined` (does not spend the tick; new `Submit::submitted()`), returned for a refinement repeat, which leaves the capture thread armed;
  - `Encoder` holds `repeats` and records fresh or refined after ProcessInput;
  - `collect` calls `output`, reading MFSampleExtension_VideoEncodeQP only while refining or after `read_qp()`: the low 16 bits, with 0 and values over 51 treated as none;
  - `set_rate` stores the pace and budget, pending units became an `InFlight` struct, and `Encoded` gains `refined` and `qp`;
  - `Statistics` gains `refine` and `refined`; `EncoderOptions::refinement` takes `Refinement::{Auto, On, Off}`;
  - `REFINE_ENCODERS` (vendor ID, MFT name fragment) is empty, so sessions are unchanged; `desktop_video_encoder_opened` logs `refine`.
- video/codec.rs: the exhaustive `EncoderOptions` destructure takes the new field.
- platform/windows/mod.rs, backend.rs, worker/window.rs, codec/pipeline.rs and protocol.rs: doc comments only. protocol.rs now explains what `duplicate` means.
- worker/tests.rs: the armed-capture fake models refinement. New test `a_refinement_burst_keeps_the_tick_armed_for_the_next_present` runs thread C end to end. It fails if a refinement repeat spends the tick.
- examples/video_bench.rs:
  - `--text --freeze <ms>`: the text page scrolls 4 rows a refresh, then freezes. Every unit after the freeze prints a `still_unit` line (index in --output, ms, bytes, duplicate, keyframe, refined, qp), plus a `still` summary.
  - `--refine on|off`.
  - The capture line reports `refine` and `refined`.
  - A `Refined` outcome counts as a submitted sample for --dump-source and as a poll.
- Docs:
  - docs/remote-desktop.md: a Windows refinement paragraph, the Mac's liveness-only note, a constants row, the diagnostics for presented_fps, present_interval, empty_polls_per_s and refine, and the per-vendor device runs under "Encoder rate model per GPU".
  - docs/architecture.md: a line for refine.rs.
  - New record docs/benchmarks/2026-11-24-still-refinement/ (README.md, policy-tests.txt, windows-check.txt, vt_still_refine.swift, vt_still_refine.txt), indexed in docs/README.md.
  - CHANGELOG.md: an SDK bullet under Unreleased, with the measured Mac figures.

No wire, ALPN, HELPER_PROTOCOL, FFI or viewer change: the helper's v10 `submitted: false` already carries Refined.

impl.measurements:
Mac only. Release Swift probe (swiftc -O) on an Apple M6 with 12 cores and 24 GiB, macOS 27.0 (26A425), with other builds running (load average 2.5-4). Raw data: docs/benchmarks/2026-11-24-still-refinement/vt_still_refine.txt and vt_still_refine.swift.

Setup: VideoToolbox configured like the Mac host's encoder (low-latency rate control, 1080p, nominal 60, 4 Mbit/s with a 1.5x/1 s cap, wall-clock pts). Text scrolls for 1 s, then stops; repeats run for 2 s. Three trials per arm.

H.264:
- Liveness repeats every 250 ms from 250 ms:
  - 35.4-35.9 dB at 250 ms (still the scroll's last unit);
  - 36.1-39.0 dB at 500 ms;
  - 42.9-46.6 dB at 1000 ms;
  - best 49.0-49.1 dB, within 0.5 dB of it at 1001-1260 ms;
  - 314-323 KB of repeats.
- Burst of 15 repeats 16.7 ms apart from 200 ms, then liveness:
  - 39.2-41.9 dB at 250 ms;
  - 41.2-43.2 dB at 500 ms;
  - 45.8-48.6 dB at 1000 ms;
  - best 48.9-49.0 dB, within 0.5 dB of it at 943-1193 ms;
  - 293-355 KB of repeats.
- Inside the burst, the first three repeats took 108-125 KB together. Most later repeats were 84-550 B. The policy's size stop would end each burst at its 7th repeat.

H.265: the scroll's last unit was already 51.8-52.2 dB. Repeats of 118-133 B moved it by at most 0.1 dB.

Windows: none measured (needs a GPU).

